        {
          "id": "s1",
          "text": "Gather and prepare all ingredients.",
          "ingredientRefs": []
        },
        {
          "id": "s2",
          "text": "Bring a large pot of water to a boil over high heat. Add {i1} and continue to boil until tender (7-10 minutes). Drain the pasta in a colander.",
          "ingredientRefs": [
            "i1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s3",
          "text": "While {i1} is cooking, prepare the creamy tomato sauce. Dice {i2} and mince {i3}. Add the onion, garlic, and {i4} to a large skillet and sauté over medium heat until the onions are soft and translucent (3-5 minutes).",
          "ingredientRefs": [
            "i1",
            "i2",
            "i3",
            "i4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s4",
          "text": "Add {i5} (with juices), {i6}, {i7}, {i8}, {i9}, and some freshly cracked pepper to the skillet. Stir to combine. Add {i11} and a 1/2 cup (125ml) of {i12} to the skillet and stir until the tomato paste has mixed into the sauce.",
          "ingredientRefs": [
            "i5",
            "i6",
            "i7",
            "i8",
            "i9",
            "i11",
            "i12"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s5",
          "text": "Turn the heat down to low. Cut {i13} into a few pieces and then add them to the skillet with the tomato sauce. Use a whisk to stir the sauce until the cream cheese has fully melted and the sauce is creamy. Add {i14} to the skillet and stir until it is melted into the sauce.",
          "ingredientRefs": [
            "i13",
            "i14"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s6",
          "text": "Add {i15} to the skillet and gently stir it into the sauce until it has wilted (2-3 minutes). Add {i1} and stir until it is well coated in the creamy tomato sauce. Taste and adjust {i9} and pepper as needed. Serve warm.",
          "ingredientRefs": [
            "i1",
